@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# Timed sleep-screen refresh
+
+This integration candidate combines the existing local wallpaper consumer with
+one SD-plugin consumer. It is dependent review code, not a capability available
+in every official CrossPoint release. It builds on the timer work in #3820,
+jadehawk's local timed-refresh implementation, and the PaperMono SDK RTC work.
+
+## Choose one source
+
+In Display settings, **Sleep refresh source** selects:
+
+- **Off:** no timer refresh is armed, even when a wallpaper interval or plugin
+  handler is configured.
+- **Local wallpapers:** rotates valid BMP files from `/.sleep` using the Custom
+  sleep-screen bitmap renderer and the local refresh interval. It does not use
+  `/sleep.bmp` or the legacy `/sleep` directory. This path does not start Wi-Fi. The sleep-screen
+  mode must be Custom. The timer path begins in native portrait orientation;
+  saved fit/crop and bitmap filter preferences still apply.
+- **SD plugin:** uses one qualified `sleep.timer` handler and its interval. It
+  requires the Plugin System to be enabled, a supported model, a valid trust
+  anchor and saved token, and a saved Wi-Fi network. Missing or conflicting
+  configuration keeps the timer off. The network prototype is limited to
+  Sticky, X4 Pro and PaperMono.
+
+The setting is stored as `timedSleepSource`: 0=Off, 1=Local, 2=Plugin. An absent
+field preserves an existing nonzero local interval as Local. A malformed or
+out-of-range explicit field is Off. New installations default to Off; installing
+an event manifest alone does not enable network wake. These names and values
+remain a proposed upstream contract until accepted.
+
+The source chooses the autonomous timer consumer. Ordinary sleep screens,
+reader events and manually opened plugins retain their existing behavior.
+A failed selected source never falls back to another source's image.
+On boards that normally go straight to sleep after a USB-powered cold boot,
+an explicitly selected refresh source is rearmed. Off keeps the normal untimed
+sleep; boards that stay awake on USB keep their existing behavior.
+Local wakes do not load or save reader state or wallpaper history, so a random
+image may repeat. A missing or invalid `/.sleep` image leaves the panel unchanged;
+the configured local interval can still rearm. An initial bitmap decode failure
+also leaves the panel unchanged. Grayscale uses the existing multi-pass renderer:
+a failure in a later gray pass can leave the completed black-and-white base.
+
+## Reading and failure behavior
+
+The timer wake does not launch a reader activity or write book progress. A
+captured Power request returns through normal reader wake handling, including
+the configured click/hold preference. The GPIO path retains pressed and verified
+states across blocking work; PaperMono uses its PMIC's read-clear button event.
+An unexpected return from shutdown uses the existing recovery path rather than
+continuing with powered-down peripherals.
+
+For SD plugins, transient network, certificate or BMP failures preserve the
+last-good asset and do not request a new panel transfer. Missing configuration
+disables arming; a transient attempt failure can rearm the same configured
+interval. The network's 20% battery threshold is prototype policy. It does not
+apply to local rotation and is not a measured battery-life guarantee.
+
+The interval is sleep time. Boot, transfer, decoding and panel work add to the
+full cycle. The network join and attempt budgets are cooperative, not hard
+bounds for every SDK or display operation. A retained image cannot update its
+own offline label; a service should include an explicit generation time.
+
+## Validation boundaries
+
+Host tests exercise the actual source/settings preparation, transport, timer
+orchestration, typed Power capture, arm/cancel and returned-shutdown paths.
+TLS loopback checks use the actual SDK transport and BMP decoder. These do not
+measure SD power-loss durability, physical button timing, battery energy or
+all device models. Hardware results belong to the exact tested binary and
+model in the review notes. Do not combine two independently armed timer callers
+or treat the local wallpaper consumer as proof of online delivery.
