+++ b/test/timer_plugin_permission/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Timer permission bootstrap checks
+
+The runner compiles the actual narrow settings method and plugin discovery, plus
+the unchanged extracted timer preflight. Storage uses a temporary filesystem;
+Wi-Fi credentials and event selection are controlled boundaries. It checks
+explicit enable/disable, malformed/absent/null settings, legacy detection,
+quarantine and root priority, read/SD failure, the 16 KiB limit and ordinary-sleep
+RAM behavior. Assertions remain active in Release. No settings file is written
+by the production method.
+
+Use `python3 test/timer_plugin_permission/run.py --arduinojson /path/to/ArduinoJson/src`.
+An optional `--baseline-main` accepts the exact pre-bootstrap main.cpp and
+confirms that it cannot discover the enabled plugin on cold timer boot (exit 42).
+These are source/host checks, not battery or device qualification.
+
+Malformed fields outside the permission key must also fail. The optional
+`--baseline-settings` negative control demonstrates why filtered deserialization
+is insufficient: a discarded malformed numeric value can be skipped as valid.
+The final reader validates the whole bounded JSON and assigns only permission.
